People keep repeating that robotics is still years away from anything meaningful. But those who are paying attention know that the leap has already happened. Just take a look at what @openmind_agi is delivering in the real world.

With the #OpenMind OM1 software running inside, this robot wasn’t just standing around at F1 , it was engaging, responding, understanding context, and interacting with guests like a natural part of the environment. Not a scripted demo. Not a lab illusion. A glimpse into how intelligent machines behave when autonomy becomes innate.

We’ve crossed the point where humanoids are just experimental prototypes. We are now entering the phase where they learn from us, work alongside us, and integrate into our daily lives.

A world where robots are not future concepts, but future citizens.

The question isn’t if this will happen , it’s whether we’re ready for the moment when they become our colleagues, our assistants, and maybe even our collaborators in discovery.

Are you prepared to coexist with the next intelligent species?
